{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011ChK51VC1Cs6qcqZHoM6po","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed `titleCase` in `strings.js`, but I could not run it. The PowerShell tool was denied in this session, so the check below is by reading only.\n\nThe bug was that the function only uppercased the first character of the whole string, so `\"hello world\"` became `\"Hello world\"`. The new version uppercases the first character of every whitespace-separated word:\n\n```js\nfunction titleCase(s) {\n  return s.replace(/\\S+/g, (word) => word.charAt(0).toUpperCase() + word.slice(1));\n}\n```\n\n- `\"hello world\"` → `\"Hello World\"`\n- Runs of spaces and leading or trailing whitespace are preserved, since the regex only touches non-space runs.\n- Empty string returns `\"\"`.\n\nI kept the existing behaviour of not lowercasing the rest of each word, so `\"hELLO\"` stays `\"HELLO\"`. If you want the usual title-case normalisation, that is a one-line change.\n\nI have not run a test. To check it yourself, run `node -e \"const {titleCase}=require('./strings.js'); console.log(titleCase('hello world'))\"` from the project directory. The project is not a git repository, so there is no diff to review, and I did not add a test file."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":421,"cache_read_input_tokens":23751,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":421},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cafd8bbe-a307-4d16-b4b6-4a811872873d","uuid":"b0009ee0-544f-466a-94b1-747ebf361d63","timestamp":"2026-11-23T02:27:38.636Z","request_id":"req_011ChK51V2pP2SmPsTYzxL6n"}
